WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.330
Speaker 1: Lawyers are increasingly predicting
that failed former President Donald Trump

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.120
is inevitably going to be indicted.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.800
And we're going to look at one of those op
eds momentarily.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.830
Now, there are many people asking if Trump
is indicted.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:20.840
Is he going to be arrested and perp walk than
booked at a federal prison the way that many

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.099
so-called normal people are?

00:00:23.099 --> 00:00:24.900
And I believe the answer is obviously not.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.630
And we're going to get back to that in a moment.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:30.220
But let's first start with the case that is
increasingly being made.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.640
Very interesting article in The Daily Beast
by Brad Moss, who says it's over.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.270
Trump will be indicted.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.230
The case is as follows.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:45.270
Brad Moss says Donald Trump will be indicted
by a federal grand jury and he believes that

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.920
the reason for that is as follows.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.370
Number one, Trump was in unauthorized possession
of national defense information, namely, properly

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.570
marked classified documents.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.100
Number two, Trump was put on notice by the
U.S. government that he was not permitted

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.760
to retain those documents at Mar a Lago.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:09.480
And number three, Trump continued to maintain
possession of the documents and allegedly

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:14.780
undertook efforts to conceal them in different
places throughout the property up until the

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:19.300
FBI finally executed a search warrant earlier
this month.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:22.710
And Moss says this is the ballgame, folks.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:28.610
Absent some unforeseen change in factual or
legal circumstances, he believes there is

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.810
little left for the Justice Department to
do.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:37.430
But to decide, do you indict before the midterms
or after the midterms in terms of what you

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.590
ask for the grand jury?

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:43.690
And as Moss also points out, the cruelest
irony for Trump is it never needed to be this

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:44.690
way.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:45.690
And that's a theme with Donald Trump.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:51.820
Much of the problems that Donald Trump gets
into, many of the problems are a result of

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:54.680
Trump's own doing and self-inflicted harm.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.460
So let's now think this through.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.540
If Trump is indicted, will he be arrested?

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.620
Book perp walk that a federal prison?

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.690
The answer is almost certainly not.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:07.390
Donald Trump will almost certainly be given
the opportunity to present himself to the

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.890
FBI on his own terms.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:15.560
And it's all going to be handled in a very
different way than it is with so-called mere

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.560
mortals.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.190
And I use that term extraordinarily sarcastically.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:25.450
Now, there is a counterpoint to that, which
is when you look at what Trump is being investigated

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:31.230
for, based on all of the documents that we
now have, when you're talking about Espionage

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:37.660
Act violations, you often don't give those
people a chance to turn themselves in.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:38.730
You arrest them.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:43.280
And that's an absolutely perfectly natural
analysis.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.680
But it's Trump.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.680
It's Trump.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.430
And we have to set our expectations correctly.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:51.740
The FBI and Secret Service would almost certainly
just coordinate the delivery of Trump to the

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.860
Justice Department.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:59.459
Trump will probably be, by the way, I you
know, if and let's not get ahead of ourselves,

00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:03.209
if and when this happens, it's going to be
a historic and historic moment.

00:03:03.209 --> 00:03:06.770
It's going to be both in American history,
unquestionably.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:10.290
And they will say it's unprecedented and that
means it's wrong.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.780
Well, no, Trump did things.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:12.780
No president did.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:16.610
So now the outcomes are also different than
they were with any other president.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.610
But.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:22.750
Donald Trump is almost certainly going to
fundraise off of this if Donald Trump is indicted

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.849
and he's given some bail amount.

00:03:24.849 --> 00:03:27.239
He is going to fundraise off of it.

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:31.500
It's going to be absolutely incredible to
see Donald Trump doing this.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:38.599
So I think if we want to be as realistic as
possible, I would put out of your minds that

00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:42.599
you're going to see Trump in an orange jumpsuit
behind bars.

00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:45.510
I would bet anything I have that that's not
going to happen.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:52.319
I'm with you that Trump and the people around
him who were complicit in what are now countless

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:55.550
instances of wrongdoing, they deserve to be
prosecuted.

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:58.550
And if found guilty in prison, there's no
doubt about it.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.489
But even just think about it.

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:05.069
I mean, Trump in a federal prison, like even
if it was even if it was plausible that Trump

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:11.340
would be sentenced, it is a national security
risk to have a former president in a federal

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.340
prison.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.519
It's an insane conversation that we're even
having.

00:04:14.519 --> 00:04:20.069
But if I think ahead, five, six, seven, eight
steps and I think about if there are charges

00:04:20.069 --> 00:04:27.139
and if there's a conviction or a plea deal
that involves some kind of serious consequence,

00:04:27.139 --> 00:04:30.280
it's Trump restricted to one of his luxury
clubs, right?

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.130
I mean, I think we would all probably agree
that's the direction it goes.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.770
But the big headline is not that that's speculative.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:36.880
That's about the future.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.669
The big headline is lawyers increasingly believe
Trump is going to be indicted.

00:04:40.669 --> 00:04:44.990
And the growing question is, what exactly
is Donald Trump's legal defense going to be?

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.240
And that's what I want to talk about next

